  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mexico Institutional Strengthening of Congress - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an Institutional Development Fund to support a second phase program of reforms to strengthen the institutional capacity of the Mexican Federal Congress. The overall objective of this IDF is to contribute to the strengthening of the institutional capacity of the Mexican Congress.  For this, the IDF aims at: i) systematizing legislative information under a knowledge management approach, ii) reinforcing the technical capacity of congress to generate, analyze and discuss information during the different stages of the budgetary cycle, and iii) automatization of the human resource processes.  As follow up to the first IDF grant provided to the Lower House of Representatives of Mexico, the overall objective of this IDF is to contribute to the strengthening of the institutional capacity of the Mexican Congress by supporting a second phase of internal reforms. For this purpose, the IDF aims at: i) systematizing legislative information under a knowledge management approach, ii) reinforcing the technical capacity of Congress to generate, analyze and discuss information during the different stages of the budgetary cycle, and iii) automate the human resource procedures.</narrative>
  </description>
